def dielrc(iatom, iont, temp, xpx, dirt, sig0):
    """Modification of Tim Kallman's XSTAR routine rrrec to calculate dielectronic
    recombination rates (only) to individual ionic species (modified by Omer
    Blaes 5-8-98)

    Here temp=temperature in K, xpx is the number density of atomic nuclei in
    cm^{-3} (hydrogen density=xpx/1.1, helium density=xpx*0.1/1.1),
    dirt  =the dielectronic rate in cm^3/s,
    sig0  = the value of sigma_0, the corresponding pseudo-cross-section
    iatom - atomic number (1=H, 2=He, 6=C, etc.)
    iont  - ionization stage (1 for neutrals, 2 for once ionized, etc.)

    this routine computes radiative recombination rates, both rr
    and dr.  rates are output in units of cm**3/s for each ion
    stage, where ions are numbered from 1-168:
      1=HI, 2=HeI, 3=HeII, 4=C I, 5=C II, ..., 9=C VI, 10=N I, ...,
      16=N VII, 17=O I, ..., 24=O VIII, 25=Ne I, ..., 34=Ne X,
      35=Mg I, ..., 46=Mg XII, 47=Si I, ..., 60=Si XIV, 61=S I, ...,
      76=S XVI, 77=Ar I, ..., 94=Ar XVIII, 95=Ca I, ... 114=Ca XX,
      115=Fe I, ..., 140=Fe XXVI, 141=Ni I, ... 168=Ni XXVIII.
    inputs are rate coefficients from Aldrovandi and Pequignot, Storey,
    and from Arnaud and Raymond for iron

    Corresponds to tlusty208.f lines 37482-37860 (subroutine dielrc)
    Modifies scalar dummies DIRT, SIG0 → returns all scalar dummies (iatom, iont, temp, xpx, dirt, sig0)
    """
    NNI = 168                    # parameter (nni=168)
    CONS = 0.1239529 * 3.28805e15 / 13.595   # parameter (cons=...)

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # DATA statements (all read-only, never modified) → assigned directly at the top of the function.
